# Stack assumptions

- Next.js 16.x App Router.
- React 19.3.
- TypeScript with strict mode.
- Tailwind CSS 4.x for utilities and tokens.
- shadcn/ui only as composable primitives, not as the visual identity.
- Motion for React for most UI motion; use GSAP only for interactions that genuinely need timeline-level control.

# Architecture

- Prefer Server Components by default.
- Add `use client` only at interactive boundaries.
- Keep domain components in feature/domain folders rather than putting everything under generic UI.
- Keep data access behind repository/service interfaces so demo data and Supabase can be swapped without rewriting the UI.
- Avoid client-side fetching when server rendering or server actions are sufficient.
- Use accessible semantic HTML before styling.
- Keep route handlers and server actions thin; business logic belongs in services.
